<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bathoen I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1910">1910</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bathoen I was chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangwaketse">Bangwaketse</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tswana-people">Tswana people</a> of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>, from 1889 until his death in 1910, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanye">Kanye</a>. In 1895 he travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khama-iii">Khama III</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sebele-i">Sebele I</a> to oppose the planned transfer of the Bechuanaland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cecil-rhodes">Cecil Rhodes</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-south-africa-company">British South Africa Company</a>, and their campaign persuaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colonial-office">Colonial Office</a> to keep the protectorate under the Crown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bathoen-i.jpg" alt="Bathoen I" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Most likely Edwin Lloyd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bathoenicirca1895.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
